course: dictionary
lesson: 13087
title: Filtration: catching the solid bits
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Filtration separates solid bits from a liquid or gas. You pour the mixture through a filter, and the liquid or gas gets through while the solid bits stay behind. «Ruby poured the muddy water through the paper filter, and the mud stayed on the paper.» Here filtration separated the mud from the water.
explain: A filter can be paper, sand or cloth. Each one has tiny gaps. Water and air can slip through the gaps, but the bigger solid bits get trapped. «The sand filter caught the grains of dirt before the water reached the tap.»
explain: Filtration does not remove everything. «Salt dissolves in water and passes through the filter paper, so the water still tastes salty.» Dissolved salt needs a different method, called evaporation. Before you choose a method, ask: is the thing I want to remove a solid bit, or is it dissolved?
fact: Filtration means separating solid bits from a liquid or gas by passing it through a filter.
fact: Filters can be made of paper, sand or cloth.
fact: «Water filtration» means cleaning water by passing it through filters.
fact: Water treatment plants use filtration to make water safe to drink.
fact: Filtration cannot remove dissolved salt; that needs evaporation.
exercise: «Ruby poured the muddy water through a filter, and the mud stayed behind.» What process separated the mud from the water? | Dissolving | *Filtration | Condensation | Evaporation
exercise: «The water plant uses filtration to clean river water before it reaches homes.» Why does the plant use filtration? | To add salt to the water | To make the water warmer | *To clean the water by passing it through filters | To turn the water into steam
exercise: Which of these is a material a filter can be made of? | Steam | Sugar | Salt | *Cloth
test: Sam mixes sand and water and wants to separate them. Which method should he use? | *Filtration through filter paper | Boiling until the water is gone | Adding more sand | Stirring hard
test: Salty sea water is passed through filter paper. Is the salt removed? | No, because salt is a gas | *No, dissolved salt passes through and needs evaporation | Yes, but only the big grains | Yes, filtration removes all the salt
exam: Which statement about filtration is correct? | *Filtration separates solid bits from a liquid or gas by passing it through a filter | Filtration turns a liquid into a solid | Filtration only works on sound | Filtration removes dissolved salt from water
